    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12331855/comment/12373837",
          "id": "12373837",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=angela",
            "name": "angela",
            "key": "anchela",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Angela Schreiber",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "hi julian\n\nif i remember correctly, the reason for this is that JSR170 does not allow to perform a 'shallow' copy.\nthe conflict would be detected by the javax.jcr.Workspace#copy therefore no additional check for existing parent is performed.\n\nIf you think this is worth an extra check, i would add it to the AbstractWebdavServlet, where some basic validation of the destination is done.\n\nregards\nangela",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=angela",
            "name": "angela",
            "key": "anchela",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Angela Schreiber",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2006-04-10T18:19:51.000+0000",
          "updated": "2006-04-10T18:19:51.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12331855/comment/12373842",
          "id": "12373842",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=reschke",
            "name": "reschke",
            "key": "reschke",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677"
            },
            "displayName": "Julian Reschke",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "Angela,\n\nconfirmed: modifying the Litmus test case to use Depth: Infinity shows that in this case the correct response code is returned. Will investigate further.\n\nBest regards, \n\nJulian ",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=reschke",
            "name": "reschke",
            "key": "reschke",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677"
            },
            "displayName": "Julian Reschke",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "created": "2006-04-10T19:43:29.000+0000",
          "updated": "2006-04-10T19:43:29.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12331855/comment/12374214",
          "id": "12374214",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=reschke",
            "name": "reschke",
            "key": "reschke",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677"
            },
            "displayName": "Julian Reschke",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "OK, as Angela pointed out, this is because Litmus is trying a shallow copy, which currently isn't implemented. Returning 403 in this case is correct.\n\nHowever, there seems to be a very simple workaround which does not only make Litmus happy, but may also help in some real-world cases: only reject the request here if the source resource indeed is a collection (otherwise WebDAV semantics for Depth: 0 and Depth: Infinity are identical).\n\n(attached)",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=reschke",
            "name": "reschke",
            "key": "reschke",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677"
            },
            "displayName": "Julian Reschke",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "created": "2006-04-13T00:42:22.000+0000",
          "updated": "2006-04-13T00:42:22.000+0000"
        },
